<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Klas takes part in **no** platform backup or transfer. `android:allowBackup="false"` in the manifest
  already says so; this file says it again for Android 12+, where cloud backup and device-to-device
  transfer are governed here, so the intent is stated rather than inferred from one attribute.

  Three reasons, in order of what they cost:

  1. **It would contradict what the app is.** Klas is offline-first and local-only: no backend, no
     account, no network calls, and so no privacy policy to write. Auto Backup *is* a network call —
     it copies klas.db to Google's servers. That database holds every student's name, phone number and
     email address, and the transfer would have to be declared on Play's Data safety form. The app was
     designed not to need that conversation.

  2. **A restored database would be quietly wrong.** Auto Backup copies the file; it does not run the
     app's own restore path (`data/backup/BackupRestore`), which exists because restoring is more than
     rows: reminders have to be re-planned and lessons re-mirrored to *this* device's calendar. Every
     `classes.calendar_event_id` in a transferred database points at an event in the old phone's
     calendar, so the mirror would go on updating and deleting nothing, for ever, with nothing on
     screen to say so. Settings are device-local by design and would come back regardless, including
     `onboardingComplete`.

  3. **The copy might not even be sound.** Room runs SQLite in WAL mode, and Auto Backup copies the
     database while the app may be writing, with no checkpoint — the documented way to restore a torn
     database.

  What replaces it is deliberate rather than absent: the tutor exports a versioned JSON snapshot
  through SAF, to storage they chose, and first-run onboarding offers to restore one. That path is
  checked before it writes a row (`BackupIntegrity`), and it re-plans reminders and re-mirrors the
  calendar afterwards.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
